# Allowlist: only the AI study and the Realidea files we modify are tracked.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/_AI-Study/
!/Realidea V4.1/
/Realidea V4.1/*
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/
/Realidea V4.1/Data/*
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/Scripts.rxdata
# the two PBS files the gen 7 learnset merge rewrote (tools/learnset_merge.py); every
# other PBS file is the game's own and stays untracked
!/Realidea V4.1/PBS/
/Realidea V4.1/PBS/*
!/Realidea V4.1/PBS/pokemon.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/PBS/tm.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/ai_scenarios.txt
# Live play against the Foul Play search: the two switches that turn it on, and the
# native sidecar the game starts itself (built by _AI-Study/tools/build_sidecar_exe.sh --
# rebuild and recommit it after any change to foul_play_sidecar.py or the engine patch).
# The switches only apply in live play: the gauntlet and probe wrap every battle in
# with_config, which neither reads them nor auto-starts the exe. A worker copied from
# this Data/ still carries portable_ai.txt, so delete it there before a measured run.
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/portable_ai.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/ai_harness.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/FoulPlay/
# mkxp-z's player config: starts fullscreen (Alt+Enter toggles) and F12 resets the game
!/Realidea V4.1/mkxp.json
# the player-curve switches (PLAYER-CURVE.md): tracked so a pull turns them on
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/level_cap_mode.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/wild_scaling.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/badge_rewards.txt
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/player_services.txt
# the data the PBS compiles into, committed with the PBS so a pull needs no compile
# (the mkxp-z player never compiles; tools/compile_pbs_bundle.py forces one)
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/attacksRS.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/berryplants.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/connections.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/dexdata.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/eggEmerald.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/encounters.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/evolutions.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/items.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/metadata.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/metrics.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/moves.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/phone.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/regionals.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/shadowmoves.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/tm.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/townmap.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/trainerlists.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/trainers.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/trainertypes.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/types.dat
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/Constants.rxdata
!/Realidea V4.1/Data/messages.dat
# The one-double-click launcher (sidecar + game). The trigger files it creates
# stay untracked on purpose: a committed Data/portable_ai.txt would be copied
# into the gauntlet workers, and a measured run with the marker present makes
# both arms portable and invalidates the stock/portable pairing.
!/Realidea V4.1/Play with Foul Play.bat
__pycache__/

# Foul Play bridge build products (tools/build_poke_engine.sh): a venv and a clone.
_AI-Study/generated/foul_play/
# Dex cache dumped out of the (untracked) pokemon-showdown clone by
# tools/dump_showdown_dex.js. Rebuilt on demand by tools/mono_synergy.py.
_AI-Study/generated/showdown_dex.json
pokemon-showdown/
# Run & Bun battle harness (tools/rnb/setup_battles.sh): foul-play clone + venv, the
# pokemon-showdown npm install, and the raw bot logs (~120 MB per full run).
_AI-Study/generated/rnb_work/
# Showdown pokedex cache fetched by tools/rnb/paths.py.
_AI-Study/generated/rnb/pokedex.json
